 <entry>
  <id>yt:video:zx8yjYHZxMg</id>
  <yt:videoId>zx8yjYHZxMg</yt:videoId>
  <yt:channelId>UCblfuW_4rakIf2h6aqANefA</yt:channelId>
  <title>Attempting The Longest Set Of Monkey Bars Ever Built LIVE</title>
  <link rel="alternate" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zx8yjYHZxMg"/>
  <author>
   <name>Red Bull</name>
   <uri>https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCblfuW_4rakIf2h6aqANefA</uri>
  </author>
  <published>2026-10-26T09:25:19+00:00</published>
  <updated>2026-11-02T10:00:29+00:00</updated>
  <media:group>
   <media:title>Attempting The Longest Set Of Monkey Bars Ever Built LIVE</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/zx8yjYHZxMg?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/zx8yjYHZxMg/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Thomas van Tonder is taking monkey bars to the next level and attempting the longest set of monkey bars ever built. The course is attached underneath Africa's highest bridge, and follows the natural arch of the bridge meaning that he will have to also overcome the challenge of the change in elevation as the lactic acid in his arms builds up.

The course is 280 meters long, and there are approximately 600 different bars for Thomas to traverse in his attempt to cross to the other side. 

The bridge is 216 meters high and is the highest bridge in Africa 📐

